📍 Level 1: Data Foundations & Exploratory Analysis
This level focuses on the critical first steps of the data pipeline: cleaning raw data, uncovering hidden patterns, and translating numbers into initial visual stories using three distinct datasets.

🛠️ Task Breakdown
Task 1: Data Cleaning and Preprocessing
Dataset: Social Media Sentiment Data

Objective: Transform "noisy" social media text and metadata into a structured format for analysis.

Key Actions:

Handled missing values and removed duplicate entries.

Standardized timestamps and cleaned text data (removing special characters/emojis).

Label encoding for categorical sentiment tags.

Tools: Python (Pandas).

Task 2: Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
Dataset: Telecom Customer Dataset

Objective: Identify the primary drivers behind customer attrition (Churn).

Key Actions:

Analyzed the correlation between Customer Service Calls and Churn Rate.

Discovered a "Churn Spike" after the 3rd service call.

Segmented usage patterns (Day vs. Night calls) to find behavioral outliers.

Tools: Python (Matplotlib, Seaborn).

Task 3: Basic Data Visualization
Dataset: Iris Flower Dataset

Objective: Apply multi-variate visualization techniques to a classic classification dataset.

Key Actions:

Created Pair Plots to visualize the relationship between sepal and petal dimensions.

Used Box Plots to identify outliers in species measurements.

Generated a Heatmap to show strong feature correlations.

Tools: Seaborn, Pandas.

📈 Level 1 Outcomes
Established a high standard for data hygiene (Data Cleaning).

Translated raw behavioral data into actionable business thresholds (Telecom EDA).

Mastered the ability to visualize complex relationships in multi-dimensional data (Iris Visualization).
